WEBVTT

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.200
The following tale is a work of pure fiction.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:50.090
Indeed, Milord concocts the most intriguing of ideas.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.320
Ingenious, is marching through Kyoto and presenting our forces to the Emperor.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.180
In my most fitting visage... {kakunaru ue wa}

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:08.020
I shall steel myself for this rare opportunity of parading steeds!

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.740
<b>Kind of Black {ts}</b>

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.490
<b>February 1581 {ts}</b>

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.490
<b>Kyoto {ts}</b>

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.240
Belated, are ye masters.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:52.450
Leading the fore, General Akechi and the other generals passed through quite some time ago. {until gozaimasu}

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:57.070
Though through haste, the flocks had impended our pace.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:14.250
Milord appears ever festive this day.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.760
As Milord should.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.670
The Hojo clan is now allied to Milord,

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.770
and the Ikko-ikki have all but surrendered to Milord's might.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.860
Through the modest invasions of Kaga and Echizen, Milord's strength flourished.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.260
This parade holds significant meaning for Milord's achievements.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:37.720
Through this parade may others know that Milord truly controls the nation. {until dekimasukara na}

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:45.010
Perhaps we should leave through the rear alley in order to reach the fore of the parade. {until dekimasu ga}

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.630
'Tis brilliant insight.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.900
Should we lose sight of their visages, {until atte wa}

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:54.130
we forgo the prospect of trading fashionable garments to other competitors.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.160
Your parchments pique my curiosity.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:03.640
Naught but assessments up to a total of five, based on each general's overall attire.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:10.170
The general whose attire is most fashionable shall bring good revenue to garment trade.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:14.780
For instance, take General Akechi's assessment of four.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:26.960
His pale jade hood suits his overall attire, as well as the white coat of the horse.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:33.030
Though General Akechi approaches 60, his attire is naught but calm and refreshing.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:40.240
Though leading the parade, General Akechi is under immense pressure to ensure it's success. {until iu no ni}

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.170
And yet, he is admired for his humble and refined disposition.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:46.630
Indeed.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:50.190
General Akechi has already determined the standard for my trade.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.910
General Akechi is my trusted confidant.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.940
His choice of attire shall be exclusive to my trade, alone.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.340
Nay shall I thieve.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.900
The unfortunate General Shibata Katsuie's assessment of one follows General Akechi.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:12.030
The brown vest retains a hideous and absolutely filthy look about it.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:16.710
Alas, his gold scabbard does naught but further damage General Shibata's attire.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:23.580
I may hope for decent trade in the north for such garments.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:30.300
Why is there no assessment for either of those names? {until kore wa}

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:38.640
Their attires are so foreign to my eyes that I fail to assess them. {until gozaimasu}

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:46.220
Though Master Senno's advice was sound, we have arrived before the army.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:51.540
I heard General Hashiba was absent from the parade...

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.520
General Hashiba is preoccupied with subduing the Mori clan.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.430
Indeed he is.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:03.410
Most unfortunate is his absence, as he so enjoys such festivities.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.950
Look forward, Brother. {terete wa narimasenu}

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.160
Face the people with pride.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.410
I know this!

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:28.660
I've not witnessed such an attire!

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:34.430
I sympathize with Master Tsuda's hesitance to assess them!

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:37.800
From where comes the striped robes?

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.560
The robe comes from the Luzon Islands to the south.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.910
'Twas from my collection comes the robe he wears.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.300
As the robe is from the southern islands,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:53.020
perhaps the proper term for such a vivid pattern is the "tropic stripe."

00:06:58.720 --> 00:06:59.870
At last...

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:06.320
Though I've achieved few feats as a messenger by 37

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.450
and maintain a pittance of 200 koku as a governor, {until nihyaku koku}

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.590
I may partake in this parade as a true warrior.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.040
However...

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:20.330
I may display my fashionable attire before the Emperor! {until koyou to wa}

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:30.330
My beloved son and Osen, I display my soul for the nation to behold!

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.110
Hail, Furusa.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.290
You look hilarious in those garments.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:57.330
Lord Oda Nagamasu...

00:07:58.150 --> 00:08:01.150
Riding with ol' Nobunaga and my nephews was a bore,

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.990
so I wanted to see you. {from kao minikite}

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:04.840
And also... {sore ni}

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:06.460
Lord Nagamasu!

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.410
Before us! {second nagamasu}

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.120
I am to behave myself in my brother's presence.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:20.840
Lord Nagamasu's mischievous spirit has much freedom.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:24.310
Milord may administer a harsh reprimand later.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:29.530
His bold attire far exceeds the vivid robes of Governor Furuta.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.580
'Tis expected of Milord's kin.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.230
His bold attire and steed serves only as a emphasis to his true genius. {until orareru}

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:37.760
Overall, Lord Nagamasu's attire exceeds Governor Furuta's score and the total of five to earn a six.

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:39.900
Indeed.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:55.680
Farewell.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:34.380
The Emperor appeared to be enjoying the parade.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.970
Mitsuhide, ye shall be awarded for your efforts.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:40.770
If I may make a request instead of reward,

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:44.970
I ask that Milord heed the words of his kumquat vassal.

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:51.490
Regarding the exile of General Sakuma Nobumori...

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:57.800
Though he held command against the Ikko-ikki and failed in his duties, {until ni yotte}

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.050
his punishment of exile has now reached six months.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.250
Perhaps now, it is proper to pardon his failures.

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:08.090
Ye request I restore his rank?

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:10.810
Aye.

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:16.260
Ye see so little.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:21.180
His time has already passed.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:26.830
My vision for this nation is rebirth.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:33.640
There is no rebirth, should old men of his competence continue to rule.

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:37.530
Only men of my era shall reign almighty.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.720
For your contributions, he shall remain unharmed.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:47.230
Nobutada, Nobukatsu, and Nobutaka!

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:51.000
Ye marched stout with honor before the Emperor.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.080
Indeed, 'tis most proper of my sons.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.140
I shall gift unto thee.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.900
I shall gladly accept.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:01.560
I shall treasure my gift.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.810
I shall earnestly receive Father's gift.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.430
Curses...

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:43.680
Beloved...

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.560
was there anything amiss during the parade?

00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:57.700
Unfortunate...

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:13.690
that I serve, but may never surpass the kin of Milord.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:20.490
Overwhelming is this "black."

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:27.080
Though the lack of imperfections affects not the intensity...

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:30.940
the bowl is overwhelming by nature. {tada koko ni aru}

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:37.990
Master Chojiro, ye craft a masterpiece!

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:43.060
Only a true master may mold such a masterpiece. {utsuwa wa koko ni kiwamarimashita}

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:50.390
I believe my simple wares to be equal to those of Ming and Joseon.

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:56.920
On the contrary, Ming and Joseon wares pale to this simple masterpiece.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:02.730
This black tea bowl is your magnum opus!

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:14.460
<b>May 1581 {ts}</b>

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:14.460
<b>Sakai Senno Soueki's Residence {ts}</b>

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:16.960
I am pleased to have ye both this day.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.090
I should have paid ye both visits instead.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:24.160
Please Master, we are but your disciples.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:28.590
'Tis not unusual for disciples to learn in their Master's residence.

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:29.960
Aye?

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:30.630
Aye.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:36.570
This is my daughter, Ogin.

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:40.110
Good day to ye, my dear.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.570
Good day.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:49.870
Master Senno, you have my gratitude for providing the Luzon robe.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.040
'Twas indeed a splendid attire of the parade.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:55.960
I come this day to express my gratitude.

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:00.840
I have something to discuss with General Hashiba.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:06.510
Won't you and my disciple, Souji, prepare tea in the tea room?

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:09.010
Very well, Master Senno.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:14.280
I am Yamanoue Souji.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:22.280
Governor Furuta beheld the Hiragumo tea pot?

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:25.030
Indeed.

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:29.310
Though Master Souji deemed it an unworthy treasure,

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:35.980
my admiration for such a masterpiece could not expressed. {until de gozatta}

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:41.590
How naive ye are, Governor.

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:45.920
Have ye retention of the masterpieces beheld?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:50.800
I retain those I've seen in the service of Milord. {until jikishin}

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:54.760
The total beheld in this life amounts to no less than ten.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:59.260
I have beheld fifty in my lifetime.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:05.690
Ye would not fathom the number of tea ceremonies I've arranged

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.630
and distances traveled to behold such masterpieces.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:13.000
Perhaps it is unreasonable to ask the same devotion of ye. {from sono kurou until gozarimasumai}

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:16.740
However, 'twas I who assessed these pieces.

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:22.880
'Tis foolhardy to proclaim the Hiragumo a masterpiece before all others.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:28.230
He is the most unpleasant aesthete I've ever met.

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:37.080
The use of "masterpiece" began here as the standard for all craft. {until hirometamono}

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:43.100
Craft is assessed not only by appearance, but by its history and the appraiser's judgment, {until fumaete}

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.150
therein influencing the status of certain craft.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:53.550
Of those masterpieces, tea jars are the most influential.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:56.080
Curses...

00:16:56.770 --> 00:17:00.050
I am not learned in the assessment of tea jars. {until wakaranu}

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.370
I shall be chastised for ignorance...

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:11.300
Governor Furuta, know ye the most worthy of all tea jars?

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:17.990
I lack favor in wars of attrition.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:21.930
With tea, may I estrange myself from the battlefield.

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:25.440
How progresses the invasion of Mori territories?

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:30.780
During my absence from the parade, I rested well and continued negotiations,

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:32.450
therefore, the invasion progresses. {umaku ittoru}

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:36.970
The young lord, Mori Terumoto, holds little influence over his territories.  {until yowai}

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:42.240
Should we take the Inaba, Bicchu, and Hoki provinces,{until otoseba}

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:44.960
the Mori clan would be rendered frail.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:51.600
Terumoto yearns for an armistice. {until joutai yo}

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:55.470
This matter however, I keep from Milord.

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:03.560
I must display my devotion to Milord by sieging their castles. {until ikan no da}

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:07.530
Should the invasion be settled by a mere armistice, {until akechidono no you ni}

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:11.110
Milord would have me suffer as he has General Akechi.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.350
'Tis wisest.

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:26.730
Perhaps the most worthy tea jar is the Tsukumonasu in Milord's possession.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:33.110
The luster of the glaze and rounded form are all but impeccable. {until kara na}

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.940
Enough feigning. {until yosou}

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:44.150
Please tell me, Master Souji.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:52.130
The Tsukumonasu tea jar indeed retains a superb form and glaze,

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:59.890
however, there exist three tea jars which surpass it.

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:05.850
Were one to attain all three tea jars, {until naraba}

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:11.800
'twould signify the unconditional wresting of rule.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:16.710
One may rule the country with three such tea jars?! {until aru no ka}

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:27.070
Had I a father, perhaps he would resemble you.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.570
Though mere flattery, I am pleased.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:32.820
'Tis not of flattery.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:37.490
I truly feel an attraction to your powerful presence.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:44.490
We keep fine company and share our secrets.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.840
Moreso than I do with Milord.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:56.110
Though General Hashiba was not born to warriors,

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:59.240
ye became general through your own talents.

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:04.820
Though I was born to a peasant fish merchant, {until kara}

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:08.930
I became one of three tea masters of Milord.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:13.860
Perhaps we are indeed akin.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:19.370
I have but a single curiosity.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:24.620
Master Senno, why do ye incessantly indulge in black?

00:20:32.570 --> 00:20:34.950
"Black" pertains to mourning robes

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:37.380
as it does to death.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:40.250
'Tis not a commonly desired color.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:44.780
I hear not of the Barbarians or of the Ming and Joseon Dynasties {until chosen demo}

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:49.070
endorsing "black" as a desired color.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:55.700
So why does the craftsman mold for ye a black tea bowl?

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.240
There are none who would appropriate it.

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:06.790
"Black" represents my karma.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:18.720
Through my life, I notice imperfections continuing to persist, to my dismay.

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:26.200
Should such imperfections be eliminated from this world, {until habukikomimasu to}

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:31.100
only this color would remain. {until narunodesu}

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:43.530
"Black" is my ideal life.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:47.480
To live a life free of imperfection.

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:52.790
Wares from beyond our waters rule this island.

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:55.910
Were their value lost to imperfection,

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:00.800
only "black" shall remain as perfection.

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:11.460
'Tis the logic of my incessant karma.  {until gozaimasu}

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:17.430
Dare ye to impose your ideals upon the country?!

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:22.810
Not under the rule of Milord, no. {until kanaimasen}

00:22:22.810 --> 00:22:25.650
The one to manifest my karma unto the whole of the country {until jitsugen suru ni wa}

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:31.710
is one who may share my ambition.

00:22:35.950 --> 00:22:42.340
I would have ye reign to realize my ambition.

00:24:34.910 --> 00:24:36.580
<b>One's life of fifty years {ts}</b>

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:49.840
<b>There exist none who are immune to death! {ts}</b>

00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:52.010
Next time, "Strategic Incitation."

00:24:53.770 --> 00:24:58.440
Does the fork joining the warrior and aesthete truly exist?

00:24:56.730 --> 00:24:59.800
<b>Strategic Incitation {ts}</b>
